course: dictionary
lesson: 4164
title: A word from sport
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A goalkeeper is the player who stands in the goal and tries to stop the other team scoring. The word has two parts: goal, and keeper, someone who keeps the goal safe. Goalie is a short, informal word that means the same thing.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «The goalkeeper is the only player allowed to handle the ball, and only inside their own penalty area.» The words handle, penalty area and scoring tell you this sentence is about a ball game with goals.
explain: Some sentences use goalkeeper in a rule, not just to name a player. «In soccer an attacker is offside if... the goalkeeper usually counts as one» tells you that in that rule the goalkeeper counts as a defender. Read the whole sentence, not just the one hard word.
fact: A goalkeeper is the player who stands in the goal and tries to stop the other team scoring.
fact: «Goalkeepers are part of the football team, and the rules let them handle the ball in their own penalty area.»
fact: In football (soccer), the goalkeeper is the only player allowed to use their hands, and only inside their own penalty area.
fact: In hockey and ice hockey, the goalkeeper wears thick pads and a helmet.
fact: Goalie and keeper are informal words for goalkeeper.
exercise: «The goalkeeper made a brilliant save to keep the ball out of the net.» What is a save here? | Kicking the ball out of the stadium | A player sitting on the bench | *Stopping the ball from going into the goal | Scoring a goal for the other team
exercise: In football (soccer), which player is the only one allowed to handle the ball inside their own penalty area? | A defender | *The goalkeeper | A midfielder | A striker
exercise: «In a single game luck, bounces and goalkeepers can decide the score, so the scoreboard doesn't always show who played better.» What does this suggest? | The best team always wins | *A goalkeeper can change the result, so the score is not always a fair picture | Bounces only happen in hockey | Scores are never decided by players
test: What does goalkeeper mean? | A coach who plans the plays | A referee who blows the whistle | *The player who stands in the goal to stop the other team scoring | A player who scores the most goals
test: In hockey and ice hockey, what does a goalkeeper wear? | A swimming cap | Only shorts and trainers | A cape and a crown | *Thick pads and a helmet
exam: Which sentence uses goalkeeper correctly? | *The goalkeeper dived to her left and tipped the shot over the bar | My goalkeeper is a kind of ice cream | We watched the goalkeeper sing on the bus | Our goalkeeper baked a cake for the team
